  <p>The trajectory reveals three broad eras: <strong style="color:var(--text);">(1) Pre-Embargo Stability</strong> (1970–1973), where prices were administratively set below $3/bbl; <strong style="color:var(--text);">(2) The OPEC Era</strong> (1973–2000), characterized by dramatic shocks followed by mean-reverting behavior in the $10–$40 range; and <strong style="color:var(--text);">(3) The Financialized Commodity Era</strong> (2000–present), where prices broke permanently above $40 and exhibited higher absolute volatility driven by macroeconomic and speculative forces.</p>

