    --surface: #1e293b;
    --surface-alt: #334155;
    --border: #475569;
    --text: #f1f5f9;
    --text-muted: #94a3b8;
    --accent: #38bdf8;
    --accent2: #818cf8;
    --green: #4ade80;
    --red: #f87171;
    --orange: #fb923c;
    --yellow: #fbbf24;
  }}
  * {{ margin:0; padding:0; box-sizing:border-box; }}
  body {{
    font-family: 'Inter', -apple-system, BlinkMacSystemFont, 'Segoe UI', system-ui, sans-serif;
    background: var(--bg);
    color: var(--text);
    line-height: 1.7;
    padding: 0;
  }}
  .report-header {{
    background: linear-gradient(135deg, #0f172a 0%, #1e3a5f 50%, #0f172a 100%);
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border);
    padding: 3rem 2rem;
    text-align: center;
  }}
  .report-header h1 {{
    font-size: 2.2rem;
    font-weight: 700;
    letter-spacing: -0.02em;
    margin-bottom: 0.5rem;
    background: linear-gradient(135deg, var(--accent), var(--accent2));
    -webkit-background-clip: text;
    -webkit-text-fill-color: transparent;
    background-clip: text;
  }}
  .report-header .subtitle {{
    font-size: 1rem;
    color: var(--text-muted);
    max-width: 700px;
    margin: 0 auto;
  }}
  .report-header .meta {{
    margin-top: 1rem;
    font-size: 0.8rem;
    color: var(--text-muted);
  }}
  .container {{
    max-width: 1200px;
    margin: 0 auto;
    padding: 2rem;
  }}
  .kpi-grid {{
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(210px, 1fr));
    gap: 1rem;
    margin: 2rem 0;
  }}
  .kpi-card {{
    background: var(--surface);
    border: 1px solid var(--border);
    border-radius: 12px;
    padding: 1.25rem;
    text-align: center;
    transition: border-color 0.2s;
  }}
  .kpi-card:hover {{ border-color: var(--accent); }}
  .kpi-value {{
    font-size: 1.8rem;
    font-weight: 700;
    color: var(--accent);
    margin-bottom: 0.25rem;
  }}
  .kpi-label {{
    font-size: 0.8rem;
    color: var(--text-muted);
    text-transform: uppercase;
    letter-spacing: 0.05em;
  }}
  .section {{
    margin: 3rem 0;
  }}
  .section-header {{
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 0.75rem;
    margin-bottom: 1.5rem;
    padding-bottom: 0.75rem;
    border-bottom: 2px solid var(--surface-alt);
  }}
  .section-num {{
    background: var(--accent);
    color: var(--bg);
    font-weight: 700;
    font-size: 0.85rem;
    width: 32px;
    height: 32px;
    border-radius: 8px;
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    justify-content: center;
    flex-shrink: 0;
  }}
  h2 {{
    font-size: 1.5rem;
    font-weight: 600;
    letter-spacing: -0.01em;
  }}
  h3 {{
    font-size: 1.15rem;
    font-weight: 600;
    color: var(--accent);
    margin: 1.5rem 0 0.75rem;
  }}
  p {{ margin-bottom: 1rem; color: var(--text-muted); }}
  .chart-container {{
    background: var(--surface);
    border: 1px solid var(--border);
    border-radius: 12px;
    padding: 1.5rem;
    margin: 1.5rem 0;
    position: relative;
  }}
  .chart-container canvas {{
    max-height: 420px;
  }}
  .chart-title {{
    font-size: 0.9rem;
    font-weight: 600;
    color: var(--text);
    margin-bottom: 1rem;
    text-align: center;
  }}
  table {{
    width: 100%;
    border-collapse: collapse;
    margin: 1rem 0;
    font-size: 0.85rem;
  }}
  thead th {{
    background: var(--surface-alt);
    color: var(--text);
    padding: 0.75rem 1rem;
    text-align: left;
    font-weight: 600;
    font-size: 0.78rem;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    letter-spacing: 0.04em;
    border-bottom: 2px solid var(--border);
  }}
  tbody td {{
    padding: 0.6rem 1rem;
    border-bottom: 1px solid rgba(71,85,105,0.4);
    color: var(--text-muted);
  }}
  tbody tr:hover {{ background: rgba(56,189,248,0.05); }}
  .table-wrap {{
    background: var(--surface);
    border: 1px solid var(--border);
    border-radius: 12px;
    overflow: hidden;
    margin: 1rem 0;
  }}
  .stat-grid {{
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(160px, 1fr));
    gap: 0.75rem;
    margin: 1rem 0;
  }}
  .stat-item {{
    background: var(--surface);
    border: 1px solid var(--border);
    border-radius: 8px;
    padding: 1rem;
    text-align: center;
  }}
  .stat-item .val {{
    font-size: 1.3rem;
    font-weight: 700;
    color: var(--accent2);
  }}
  .stat-item .lab {{
    font-size: 0.75rem;
    color: var(--text-muted);
    margin-top: 0.25rem;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    letter-spacing: 0.04em;
  }}
  .decade-card {{
    background: var(--surface);
    border: 1px solid var(--border);
    border-radius: 12px;
    padding: 1.5rem;
    margin: 1.25rem 0;
  }}
  .decade-card h3 {{
    margin-top: 0;
    margin-bottom: 0.75rem;
  }}
  .decade-card p {{
    font-size: 0.9rem;
    line-height: 1.7;
  }}
  .callout {{
    background: rgba(56,189,248,0.08);
    border-left: 3px solid var(--accent);
    border-radius: 0 8px 8px 0;
    padding: 1rem 1.25rem;
    margin: 1.5rem 0;
    font-size: 0.9rem;
  }}
  .callout strong {{ color: var(--accent); }}
  .footer {{
    text-align: center;
    padding: 2rem;
    color: var(--text-muted);
    font-size: 0.75rem;
    border-top: 1px solid var(--border);
    margin-top: 3rem;
  }}
  .two-col {{
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr;
    gap: 1.5rem;
  }}
  @media (max-width: 768px) {{
    .two-col {{ grid-template-columns: 1fr; }}
    .report-header h1 {{ font-size: 1.5rem; }}
    .container {{ padding: 1rem; }}
    .kpi-grid {{ grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(150px, 1fr)); }}
  }}
  .toc {{
    background: var(--surface);
    border: 1px solid var(--border);
    border-radius: 12px;
    padding: 1.5rem 2rem;
    margin: 1.5rem 0;
  }}
  .toc ol {{
    padding-left: 1.25rem;
  }}
  .toc li {{
    padding: 0.3rem 0;
    color: var(--text-muted);
    font-size: 0.9rem;
  }}
  .toc a {{
    color: var(--accent);
    text-decoration: none;
  }}
  .toc a:hover {{
    text-decoration: underline;
  }}
</style>
</head>
<body>

<div class="report-header">
  <h1>Global Crude Oil Price Trends</h1>
  <div class="subtitle">A Historical Analysis of Monthly Crude Oil Prices — January 1970 to March 2026</div>
  <div class="meta">675 monthly observations &bull; Source: Kaggle Global Fuel Price Trends Dataset &bull; Prices in nominal USD/bbl</div>
</div>

<div class="container">

<!-- Table of Contents -->
<nav class="toc">
  <strong style="color:var(--text);">Contents</strong>
  <ol>
    <li><a href="#executive-overview">Executive Overview</a></li>
    <li><a href="#long-term-trend">Long-Term Price Trajectory (1970–2026)</a></li>
    <li><a href="#decade-by-decade">Decade-by-Decade Breakdown</a></li>
    <li><a href="#volatility-and-shocks">Price Volatility &amp; Major Shocks</a></li>
    <li><a href="#statistical-summary">Statistical Summary &amp; Distribution</a></li>
    <li><a href="#outlook-and-conclusions">Outlook &amp; Conclusions</a></li>
  </ol>
</nav>

<!-- ======================== SECTION 1: Executive Overview ======================== -->
<div class="section" id="executive-overview">
  <div class="section-header">
    <span class="section-num">1</span>
    <h2>Executive Overview</h2>
  </div>

  <p>This report analyzes <strong style="color:var(--text);">{s['n']} monthly observations</strong> of global crude oil prices from <strong style="color:var(--text);">{s['first_date'][:7]}</strong> to <strong style="color:var(--text);">{s['last_date'][:7]}</strong>, spanning {s['years_span']} years of energy market history. Over this period, crude oil has undergone a fundamental repricing — from $1.21/bbl in January 1970 to $87.84/bbl in March 2026 — reflecting a compound annual growth rate (CAGR) of {s['cagr']}%.</p>

  <div class="kpi-grid">
    <div class="kpi-card">
      <div class="kpi-value">${s['price_range']:.2f}</div>
      <div class="kpi-label">Overall Price Range</div>
    </div>
    <div class="kpi-card">
      <div class="kpi-value">{s['cagr']}%</div>
      <div class="kpi-label">CAGR (56.2 years)</div>
    </div>
    <div class="kpi-card">
      <div class="kpi-value">+217.1%</div>
      <div class="kpi-label">Max Monthly Change (%)</div>
    </div>
    <div class="kpi-card">
      <div class="kpi-value">{s['highest_avg_decade']}</div>
      <div class="kpi-label">Highest Avg Decade</div>
    </div>
    <div class="kpi-card">
      <div class="kpi-value">${s['std_dev']:.2f}</div>
      <div class="kpi-label">Std Deviation (full period)</div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="callout">
    <strong>Key Findings:</strong> Crude oil prices have experienced seven distinct regimes over 56 years, punctuated by geopolitical shocks (1973, 1979, 1990, 2022), demand-driven supercycles (2003–2008), supply-side disruptions (1986, 2014), and pandemic-driven collapse (2020). The all-time high of $132.83/bbl (July 2008) represents a 10,878% increase from the 1970 baseline. The overall distribution is heavily right-skewed (median ${s['median_price']}/bbl vs. mean ${s['mean_price']}/bbl), indicating that the majority of the dataset's history was spent below today's price levels.
  </div>
</div>

<!-- ======================== SECTION 2: Long-Term Price Trajectory ======================== -->
<div class="section" id="long-term-trend">
  <div class="section-header">
    <span class="section-num">2</span>
    <h2>Long-Term Price Trajectory (1970–2026)</h2>
  </div>

  <p>The chart below presents the complete monthly time series of crude oil prices. Major geopolitical and economic events are annotated to contextualize the structural inflection points that define oil's price history.</p>

  <div class="chart-container">
    <div class="chart-title">Monthly Crude Oil Price (USD/bbl) — January 1970 to March 2026</div>
    <canvas id="mainChart" height="180"></canvas>
  </div>

  <p>The trajectory reveals three broad eras: <strong style="color:var(--text);">(1) Pre-Embargo Stability</strong> (1970–1973), where prices were administratively set below $3/bbl; <strong style="color:var(--text);">(2) The OPEC Era</strong> (1973–2000), characterized by dramatic shocks followed by mean-reverting behavior in the $10–$40 range; and <strong style="color:var(--text);">(3) The Financialized Commodity Era</strong> (2000–present), where prices broke permanently above $40 and exhibited higher absolute volatility driven by macroeconomic and speculative forces.</p>

  <div class="chart-container">
    <div class="chart-title">Annual Average Crude Oil Price (USD/bbl)</div>
    <canvas id="annualChart" height="130"></canvas>
  </div>

  <p>Annual averages smooth out intra-year volatility and confirm the structural breakpoints: sub-$3 in the early 1970s, a sharp step-up to $10+ following the 1973 embargo, the 1986 reset, the 2000s supercycle to a peak annual average of $105/bbl (2012), and the post-2014 era of heightened oscillation between $40 and $100.</p>
</div>

<!-- ======================== SECTION 3: Decade-by-Decade ======================== -->
<div class="section" id="decade-by-decade">
  <div class="section-header">
    <span class="section-num">3</span>
    <h2>Decade-by-Decade Breakdown</h2>
  </div>

  <p>Grouping the data by decade reveals how the pricing environment has shifted structurally. The table and charts below compare key metrics across six decades.</p>

  <div class="table-wrap">
    <table>
      <thead>
        <tr>
          <th>Decade</th>
          <th>Observations</th>
          <th>Mean ($/bbl)</th>
          <th>Std Dev</th>
          <th>Min</th>
          <th>Max</th>
          <th>Range</th>
        </tr>
      </thead>
      <tbody>
        {"".join(f'''<tr><td style="color:var(--text);font-weight:600">{d}s</td><td>{decade_stats[d]['count']}</td><td>${decade_stats[d]['mean']}</td><td>${decade_stats[d]['std']}</td><td>${decade_stats[d]['min']}</td><td>${decade_stats[d]['max']}</td><td>${decade_stats[d]['range']}</td></tr>''' for d in sorted(decade_stats.keys()))}
      </tbody>
    </table>
  </div>

  <div class="two-col">
    <div class="chart-container">
      <div class="chart-title">Average Price by Decade</div>
      <canvas id="decadeMeanChart" height="160"></canvas>
    </div>
    <div class="chart-container">
      <div class="chart-title">Price Volatility (Std Dev) by Decade</div>
      <canvas id="decadeStdChart" height="160"></canvas>
    </div>
  </div>

  {"".join(f'<div class="decade-card"><h3>{decade_analysis[d]["title"]}</h3><p>{decade_analysis[d]["text"]}</p></div>' for d in sorted(decade_analysis.keys()))}
</div>

<!-- ======================== SECTION 4: Volatility & Shocks ======================== -->
<div class="section" id="volatility-and-shocks">
  <div class="section-header">
    <span class="section-num">4</span>
    <h2>Price Volatility &amp; Major Shocks</h2>
  </div>

  <p>This section quantifies the magnitude and frequency of extreme price movements. Volatility is measured using both rolling 12-month standard deviation and month-over-month percentage changes.</p>

  <div class="chart-container">
    <div class="chart-title">Rolling 12-Month Standard Deviation (USD/bbl)</div>
    <canvas id="volChart" height="140"></canvas>
  </div>

  <p>The rolling volatility chart reveals clear volatility clustering: the 1979–1981 revolution period, the 1986 collapse, the 2008 financial crisis (which produced the highest absolute volatility), the 2014–2016 OPEC price war, and the 2020 COVID crash. The 2000s stand out as the most persistently volatile decade overall.</p>

  <div class="chart-container">
    <div class="chart-title">Month-over-Month Price Change (%)</div>
    <canvas id="momChart" height="140"></canvas>
  </div>

  <h3>Largest Month-over-Month Price Movements</h3>
  <p>The table below shows the most extreme single-month price changes, ranked by absolute percentage change.</p>

  <div class="table-wrap">
    <table>
      <thead>
        <tr>
          <th>Month</th>
          <th>Price Before</th>
          <th>Price After</th>
          <th>% Change</th>
          <th>$ Change</th>
          <th>Event</th>
        </tr>
      </thead>
      <tbody>
        {shock_rows}
      </tbody>
    </table>
  </div>

  <div class="callout">
    <strong>Peak Monthly Shock — January 1974:</strong> The single largest monthly percentage move was +217.1%, when prices jumped from $4.10 to $13.00 following the OPEC embargo. In absolute dollar terms, the largest monthly swing was −$26.96 in October 2008, when prices fell from $99.66 to $72.69 during the Global Financial Crisis. These two records — one percentage-based, one dollar-based — reflect fundamentally different market structures: the 1974 shock hit a low-nominal market, while the 2008 crash hit prices 30× higher.
  </div>

  <h3>MoM Volatility by Decade (Std Dev of % Changes)</h3>
  <div class="chart-container">
    <div class="chart-title">Standard Deviation of Monthly % Changes by Decade</div>
    <canvas id="decadeVolChart" height="140"></canvas>
  </div>
</div>

<!-- ======================== SECTION 5: Statistical Summary ======================== -->
<div class="section" id="statistical-summary">
  <div class="section-header">
    <span class="section-num">5</span>
    <h2>Statistical Summary &amp; Distribution</h2>
  </div>

  <p>The following descriptive statistics summarize the full distribution of 675 monthly crude oil prices from 1970 to 2026.</p>

  <div class="stat-grid">
    <div class="stat-item"><div class="val">{s['n']}</div><div class="lab">Observations</div></div>
    <div class="stat-item"><div class="val">${s['mean_price']}</div><div class="lab">Mean</div></div>
    <div class="stat-item"><div class="val">${s['median_price']}</div><div class="lab">Median</div></div>
    <div class="stat-item"><div class="val">${s['std_dev']}</div><div class="lab">Std Deviation</div></div>
    <div class="stat-item"><div class="val">${s['min_price']}</div><div class="lab">Minimum</div></div>
    <div class="stat-item"><div class="val">${s['max_price']}</div><div class="lab">Maximum</div></div>
    <div class="stat-item"><div class="val">${s['p10']}</div><div class="lab">10th Percentile</div></div>
    <div class="stat-item"><div class="val">${s['p25']}</div><div class="lab">25th Percentile</div></div>
    <div class="stat-item"><div class="val">${s['p75']}</div><div class="lab">75th Percentile</div></div>
    <div class="stat-item"><div class="val">${s['p90']}</div><div class="lab">90th Percentile</div></div>
  </div>

  <div class="chart-container">
    <div class="chart-title">Price Distribution — Histogram (USD/bbl, $5 bins)</div>
    <canvas id="histChart" height="140"></canvas>
  </div>

  <p>The distribution is <strong style="color:var(--text);">strongly right-skewed</strong>. The median (${s['median_price']}/bbl) is substantially below the mean (${s['mean_price']}/bbl), indicating that the majority of monthly observations cluster at lower price levels, with a long tail driven by the 2005–2014 high-price era. The interquartile range (${s['p25']} – ${s['p75']}) spans $44.72/bbl, while the 10th-to-90th percentile range spans $77.62/bbl — reflecting the enormous variance in oil's pricing history.</p>

  <div class="callout">
    <strong>Distribution Insight:</strong> Over 50% of all monthly observations (the median) fall below $29.11/bbl. This means that for the majority of the 56-year dataset, oil was priced below what many analysts today would consider the marginal cost of production for non-OPEC producers. The high-price era (above $60/bbl) represents a fundamentally different market structure that emerged only after 2005.
  </div>
</div>

<!-- ======================== SECTION 6: Outlook & Conclusions ======================== -->
<div class="section" id="outlook-and-conclusions">
  <div class="section-header">
    <span class="section-num">6</span>
    <h2>Outlook &amp; Conclusions</h2>
  </div>

  <p>The 2020s data through March 2026 reveals a market in transition. After the pandemic crash and recovery (2020–2022), prices have entered a moderating trend — declining from over $110/bbl in mid-2022 to the $58–$73 range through most of 2025. The sharp spike to $87.84 in March 2026 introduces renewed uncertainty about near-term direction.</p>

  <h3>Key Takeaways</h3>

  <div class="decade-card" style="border-left: 3px solid var(--accent);">
    <p><strong style="color:var(--text);">1. Crude oil is a structurally volatile asset.</strong> The overall standard deviation of $30.59 represents 77% of the mean price — an extraordinary coefficient of variation. No decade has been immune to shocks of 30%+ magnitude.</p>
    <p><strong style="color:var(--text);">2. Price regimes persist, then break violently.</strong> The 1990s stability ($18.19 ± $3.82) collapsed into the 2000s supercycle ($49.17 ± $25.54). The 2011–2014 plateau above $100 broke to $30 in 18 months. Mean-reversion assumptions require time horizons of 5–10 years.</p>
    <p><strong style="color:var(--text);">3. Geopolitical events remain the dominant driver of tail risk.</strong> Of the 10 largest monthly price moves, nearly all are directly attributable to geopolitical events (embargoes, wars, revolutions) or macroeconomic crises. Supply-demand fundamentals set the trend; geopolitics determines the shocks.</p>
    <p><strong style="color:var(--text);">4. The 7.93% CAGR masks extreme path dependency.</strong> An investor exposed to this CAGR would have endured multiple drawdowns exceeding 60%, including 1985–1986 (−64%), 2008 (−69%), 2014–2016 (−72%), and 2020 (−66%). The long-term trend upward is real but the path is punishing.</p>
    <p><strong style="color:var(--text);">5. Recent moderation may not signal a new low-price era.</strong> The 2025 decline to $57.95 remains above the long-term median of $29.11 and is consistent with mid-cycle correction rather than structural repricing. The March 2026 spike demonstrates how quickly supply disruptions or demand shifts can reverse a declining trend.</p>
  </div>
</div>

</div>

<div class="footer">
  Global Crude Oil Price Trends — Historical Analysis Report &bull; Data: 675 monthly observations (Jan 1970 – Mar 2026) &bull; Source: Kaggle Global Fuel Price Trends Dataset &bull; All prices in nominal USD/bbl
</div>

